The class `ScheduledDirectPeriodicTask` is a thin wrapper around a `Runnable` that mainly forwards execution, handles disposal, and propagates errors. Its performance characteristics are dominated by the underlying `Runnable` implementation rather than any intrinsic logic in this class. Consequently, a dedicated JMH benchmark would not provide meaningful insights into the class itself, and any measurement would largely reflect the behavior of the wrapped task. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark for this specific code is unnecessary.